# Data Analysis Laboratory

The goal of this laboratory was to implement fundamental techniques for data preprocessing, data reduction, data normalization, data discretization, and data statistical analysis on the dataset 'mobsWithMissingDetails.csv.' The laboratory included random sampling to reduce the dataset size and Min-Max normalization to normalize the numerical values within the dataset, with continuous height values being discretized into different categories. Finally, the minimum, maximum, average, median, and mode have been calculated together with certain measures of dispersion, such as the range of values, quartiles, interquartiles, variance, and standard deviation. Moreover, the correlation matrix has been created using the method .corr() to see how numerical variables correlate with each other.

The statistical measures and visualizations helped to analyze the distribution of the data and its variability. The missing values for height were calculated via mean imputation before calculations were made. Random sampling was selected to obtain the data with the minimum number of records without losing important data in the dataset while Min-Max was used for data normalization. The height variable was discretized into categories to make continuous data easier to understand. One of the challenges was dealing with missing data and conducting correlation analysis only on numerical data. Overall, this laboratory confirmed that data preprocessing and statistical analysis is a good combination to help prepare and analyze datasets.